  "hypothesis_held": true,
  "conclusion": "False alarms: 0 of 6 undrifted months flagged, highest PSI 0.03130 against a 0.25 threshold, mean undrifted out-of-sample PR-AUC 0.5064. The detector is not simply flagging everything, which is what makes the delays below mean anything. covariate_shift_recency_x1.8: PSI flagged after 0 scoring month(s), max PSI 0.31099, PR-AUC 0.5538 -> 0.7079, 10% drop visible after None month(s) of matured labels, triggers ['RT-2', 'RT-3', 'RT-5', 'RT-6']. covariate_shift_one_segment: PSI flagged after 0 scoring month(s), max PSI 1.08399, PR-AUC 0.5538 -> 0.7405, 10% drop visible after None month(s) of matured labels, triggers ['RT-2', 'RT-3', 'RT-5', 'RT-6']. concept_drift_one_segment: PSI flagged after None scoring month(s), max PSI 0.03204, PR-AUC 0.5538 -> 0.3281, 10% drop visible after 0 month(s) of matured labels, triggers ['RT-1', 'RT-5', 'RT-6']. The two kinds of drift behave differently, and separating them is the result. Covariate shift is caught by PSI on the first scoring run, with no labels at all - and it does not necessarily hurt: widening a predictive feature raised PR-AUC rather than lowering it, so treating a PSI flag as evidence of damage would be wrong. Concept drift is the opposite: the feature distributions move far less, so PSI is quieter, and the harm shows only once labels mature. That is the PRD's expected observation, and it is why RT-1 and RT-4 (matured PR-AUC) exist alongside RT-2 and RT-3 (distributions): neither family of trigger would catch both cases. Status is partial: the approval half of the hypothesis is covered by the pipeline's own approval gate, not re-tested here.",
  "limitations": [
    "The approval half of the hypothesis - that the challenger is compared with the champion and promotion waits for approval - is not re-tested here. It is the approval gate of the main pipeline, covered by AT-08/AT-13 and demonstrated by scripts/run_demo.py; repeating it inside a drift experiment would measure the gate twice and the drift detectors once.",
    "Replay is over synthetic months, not Online Retail II. Only the generator can be told to shift one feature or change one segment's behaviour on demand, which is what the independent variable requires."
  ],
